\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces  Ablation study: histogram scanning kernel time per iteration (20 features, 256 bins). Column-major layout provides 1.1--2.1$\times $ speedup over the row-major baseline. The effect of u8 packing on speed is dataset-size-dependent: it improves throughput at $n = 10{,}000$ (1.4$\times $ vs.\ 1.1$\times $ for u16) but is neutral or slightly slower at $n = 1{,}000$ and $n = 100{,}000$; its primary benefit is halving memory bandwidth for bin storage. The histogram subtraction trick (not shown) reduces total tree-building work by $\sim $40\% on top of these kernel improvements.}}{12}{table.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:ablation}{{7}{12}{Ablation study: histogram scanning kernel time per iteration (20 features, 256 bins). Column-major layout provides 1.1--2.1$\times $ speedup over the row-major baseline. The effect of u8 packing on speed is dataset-size-dependent: it improves throughput at $n = 10{,}000$ (1.4$\times $ vs.\ 1.1$\times $ for u16) but is neutral or slightly slower at $n = 1{,}000$ and $n = 100{,}000$; its primary benefit is halving memory bandwidth for bin storage. The histogram subtraction trick (not shown) reduces total tree-building work by $\sim $40\% on top of these kernel improvements}{table.7}{}}
